// Simulation-based inference by DESCENT: conditioning = pinning. The posterior
// score is the free block of the JOINT score -- grad_th log p(th|d0) equals
// grad_th log p(th,d0), because log p(d0) dies under grad_th. So freeze a
// joint whose observed block sits at d0, condition with `|`, and let reverseKL
// descend the free rows onto joint simulator draws: conditional SVGD, the
// particle mirror of sbi_npse's amortized map (same toy, same three modes).
seed 7
P = sine_gaussian(2, 0.2) ~ 4000                 // joint simulator draws (rows: d, th)

// conditioned ensemble: d-block frozen at the observation, th-block = noise
(D0, TH0) = rv(couple(gaussian([0.5], 0), gaussian([0], 1))) ~ 1500
qt = descent(reverseKL(P), from=(TH0 | D0))
v = field(qt, estimator=nw(kernel=rbf))
Post = flow(v, steps=200, lr=0.3) # (TH0 | D0)

// the posterior slice sits ON the joint cloud: conditioning made visible.
// The pinned block is an OBSERVATION, not cloud geometry: both conditional
// forms ((y|x) here, (q|Obs) for observation sets) share one likelihood
// estimator with the sharp conditional-noise bandwidth, so the slice is
// taken at the simulator's noise scale, not the cloud's spread.
// quant: basin masses within 0.05 of quadrature truth, central peak
// 0.60/0.59, inter-mode valleys 0.08 (truth 0.01).
plot P, Post
